   110	# codex PARSES the tokens in auth.json as JWTs locally before sending them, so a
   111	# literal "placeholder" string is rejected ("invalid ID token format"). The
   112	# placeholder must be a VALID-FORMAT dummy JWT (header.payload.sig, base64url).
   113	# A far-future exp stops codex attempting a refresh (which the dummy refresh
   114	# token can't satisfy); the real (non-secret) account_id claim matches the
   115	# injected token's account. The dummy carries no credential -- the proxy still
   116	# replaces Authorization with the real bearer. (Confirmed live, SYD-187 go-live.)
